\date{2026-08-26}
\title{Semilattices are sets}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\import{stt-macros}
\meta{source}{\PR{249}}
\tag{changelog}

\subtree{
\title{Summary}

\p{
We formalise that the algebraic structure of a semilattice, i.e. a binary operation
#{{-}\land{-} : A \to A \to A} that is idempotent, commutative, and associative,
implies that the underlying type is a set. We use this result to slightly simplify
our development of lattices, no longer requiring an accompanying proof that the
carrier type is a set.
}

\p{
This result is due to [[davidwärn]]. Parts of the accompanying formalisation follows
[[tomdejong]]'s
[streamlined formalisation](https://martinescardo.github.io/TypeTopology/AlgebraicStructuresForcingSethood.Semilattices-streamlined.html)
in the [TypeTopology library](TypeTopology).
}
}


